WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.770
Speaker 1: In psychology projection is displacing
your feelings onto someone else.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:12.370
And in politics, or colloquially, we sometimes
call projection when you blame others for

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.700
doing something which actually you are the
one who is guilty of doing.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.730
And it's very hard to imagine any better example
of that in the modern political landscape

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:25.789
than Republicans obsessing about supposed
Democratic voter fraud, voter impersonation

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:30.831
and other hijinx when it is actually anecdotally
they themselves that they're doing it, even

00:00:30.831 --> 00:00:33.579
though overall it's extraordinarily rare.

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:39.270
We now have another example of this as a Republican
has pleaded guilty to voting in two different

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.270
states.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:46.510
And again, the big picture story is that this
type of thing is very rare, not very easy

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:52.469
to do, and has never impacted any election
to the degree that it would actually affect

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:53.639
the results.

00:00:53.639 --> 00:00:59.149
At the micro level, when individual instances
of voter fraud actually take place, it's almost

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:04.580
exclusively Republicans who are actually doing
it sometimes to, quote, test the system they

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:11.610
claim or listen, I killed them just to see
if the police are that good at solving murders.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.710
Give me a break.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:13.710
Okay.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.240
And sometimes it is because they are actually
trying to do it.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.759
They just want to vote twice or whatever the
case may be.

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:24.070
In this article, we have learned of a New
Hampshire Republican who voted in two states,

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:29.500
a man who voted in both New Hampshire and
Massachusetts in the 2016 general election

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.310
has been ordered to pay nearly $5,000 in fines
and penalties.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:40.390
Now, I think it's also important to mention
that sometimes when people have accidentally

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:43.430
voted illegally, they get prison time.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:49.109
There's a famous story of a black woman who
wasn't even deliberately voting multiple times.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.560
She just wasn't supposed to vote, and she
did.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.079
She went to jail.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:58.690
In this case tied Chrissy Ach is having to
pay a $5,000 fine.

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:03.499
Was charged in June of 2019, pleaded guilty
Friday to voting in more than one state.

00:02:03.499 --> 00:02:09.270
He was given a 90 day suspended sentence,
a $4,000 fine and a roughly thousand dollars

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.270
penalty.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:16.850
He cast ballots in Alton, New Hampshire and
Leominster, Massachusetts, on Election Day

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.590
of 2016.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:24.720
Crazy Act was registered as a Republican in
Alton, attorney David Bar Danza said his client

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.820
voted in Alton, where he lives, later visited
in mother in Massachusetts.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:34.250
She said, Hey, your name is on the list here
where he previously lived.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.100
So he went there and voted as well.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:40.240
He went down to vote thinking that he could.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.020
Does anyone believe that?

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.210
Is there any adult?

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:47.160
You know, we had this story after the in November.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:52.410
There was the Virginia gubernatorial election
where Glenn Youngkin, one, defeated Terry

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.520
McAuliffe.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:59.770
And we learned that his 17 young guns, 17
year old kid, went and tried to vote, I believe

